Description: CVE-2026-53615 - Fix integer overflow in libblkid DOS extended partition parsing
 A uint32_t integer overflow in parse_dos_extended() allows a crafted disk
 image to register a partition at sector 0 (the MBR) when cur_start + start
 wraps around. Fix by using 64-bit arithmetic for abs_start calculation,
 applying extended partition area bounds checks to all EBR data entries (not
 just index >= 2), and validating EBR link targets stay within the extended
 area and advance forward.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/commit/e9d544d013267ea86b70ee8ff78abd280e6641af
