 (non-root SUID) mounts to prevent TOCTOU race conditions where an
 attacker could replace a backing file with a symlink between path
 resolution and open(). Two vulnerabilities are addressed:
 1) loopcxt_set_backing_file() calls canonicalize_path() which uses
    realpath() and follows symlinks as euid=0.
 2) loopcxt_setup_device() opens the backing file without O_NOFOLLOW.
 .
