Description: CVE-2026-13595 - libblkid: fix use-after-free in nested partition probing
 The partitions list previously kept partitions in a contiguous array grown
 via realloc(). When the array was reallocated to a new location, existing
 blkid_partition pointers (tab->parent, ls->next_parent, locals in nested
 probers) were left dangling, causing a heap use-after-free read.
 .
 Change the storage model to an array of pointers, with each partition
 individually allocated via calloc(), so blkid_partition pointers are
 stable across reallocations. The pointer array itself may move on
 realloc(), but no code caches pointers into the pointer array.
 .
 Backport note: the target tree (util-linux 2.36.1) uses realloc() with
 manual size multiplication where upstream had switched to reallocarray().
 This backport keeps the existing realloc() call but updates the element
 size to sizeof(blkid_partition) (a pointer) to match the new
 array-of-pointers storage model.
